hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16811","Abd Allah narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah, he is al-Zubayri, narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Fa'id, the freedman of Abadil, he said: I went out with Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabi'a, and Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman sent for Ibn Sa'd until when we were at al-Arj, Ibn Sa'd came, and Sa'd is the one who guided the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the road of his riding, and Ibrahim said: Inform me of what your father narrated to you. Ibn Sa'd said: My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them, and with him was Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr had with them a daughter placed out for nursing, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to take a shortcut on the road to Medina, and Sa'd said to him: This is al-Gha'ir of Rakuba, and on it are two robbers from Aslam called al-Muhanan, and if you wish we will take them on. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take us by them. Sa'd said: So we went out until we came in sight, when one of them was saying to his companion: This is the Yamani. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them and presented Islam to them, and they accepted Islam. Then he asked them about their names, and they said: We are al-Muhanan. And he said: Rather you are al-Mukraman. And he ordered them to come to him in Medina. And we went out until we came to the outskirts of Quba, and Banu Amr ibn Awf met him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is Abu Umama As'ad ibn Zurara? And Sa'd ibn Khaythama said: He was stricken before me, O Messenger of Allah, shall I not inform him for you? Then he went on until when he came in view of the palm trees, the drinking place was full, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: O Abu Bakr, this is the dwelling; I saw myself alighting at basins like the basins of Banu Mudlij."
